<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Makerere University</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1922</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Makerere University in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampala">Kampala</a> is Uganda's oldest and largest university. Founded in 1922 as a technical school, it became Makerere College, the leading centre of higher education in British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, a college of the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> from 1949 and part of the University of East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> from 1963, before becoming an independent national university in 1970. Its alumni include <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> and many other African leaders and writers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/makerere-university.jpg" alt="Makerere University" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: OER Africa · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ssetendekero_Makerere.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
